							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1026.msg10150#msg10150"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1026.msg10150#msg10150">Not much but maybe good for a spark.</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> August 17, 2004, 01:31:50 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Daarksun<br />Guild Leader<br />65 Dark Elf Shadowknight<br /><br />First off - once again, outstanding job on Xegony. We weren&#039;t perfect - add early, 4 tank switches - but we handled it all, including the problems, wonderfully and beat her ass good. <br /><br />It&#039;s just the beginning. Some of you now realize what we are capable of doing, if you didn&#039;t already. Xegony dying was expected, not surprising. Coirnav? He&#039;s going to die first attempt. That&#039;s pretty much unheard of and you&#039;ll get laughed at if you try and tell someone as much, but mark my words - it&#039;s gonna happen. Rathe? Well.. I won&#039;t be so ballsy as to guarantee a first attempt win, but it is VERY possible. At the most, it will take a couple of attempts to get our execution down just right. <br /><br />Then on to Time. We&#039;re going to just march right through all of it, wait and see. Nothing will present a major hurdle to us and I expect most if not all of the gods to die on our first attempt. Until Quarm anyway. And we will not have the issues with him that guilds before us have had, i.e. Conviction. Why? Because we have way better gear. We have better players. Simply, Hegemony &gt; Conviction. <br /><br />But before all that good Time stuff can happen, we have a bit more work to do first. We have to finish up backflagging (it&#039;s nearly done!! ) and we have to start focusing on PoEarth and Arbitor to get everyone PoEB flagged for Rathe. This won&#039;t be a long, painful process but it does have to get done. <br /><br />In the downtime, what little of it there may be, keep working on those tipt/vxed flags - GoD progression work will begin soon as well, though it will be very light at least at the beginning. <br /><br />Now on to something else... Several guilds are opening apps again very soon if they haven&#039;t already. Conviction, EiE, Ascent and amazingly, FoT are all looking for apps. The things I&#039;m about to say mainly apply to Conviction but they apply to all of the others as well in some way, shape or form. <br /><br />Rumor has it - and I don&#039;t doubt that it is false, nor do I doubt it&#039;s true - that Conviction plans to keep us from PoTime. They also (again, rumor), plan on attempting to take some of our apps away from us. Personally, I think they give themselves way too much credit. Though I have never had any major runins with Conviction or their officers to date - well 1 long ago, the general vibe I have always gotten from them is cockiness. Being confident in your abilities is one thing, thinking you run the server is another. They (rumor..) think that they can keep a guild out of Time on a whim. They think they can snap their fingers and pick and choose people from other guilds to come join them. If any or all of that is indeed true, I think they are in for a very rude awakening. <br /><br />Now.. They primarily want clerics and bards with a few other classes and they are promising Time flags. Hell, they may even offer dkp bonuses, I don&#039;t know. But.. let me just throw out a few facts for those that might not already know. Yes, they are promising Time flags, but they are NOT backflagging Elemental flags. So though their apps may get that wonderous Time key, they will still be grinding in BoT. Second, this is their second app run in the past 4 months or so. Their last run saw them with 120+ apps as they started backflagging. Some apps were cut along the way as you would expect, but what you might not expect is what happened after those apps helped get them Time flagged - nearly all of them were cut. Basically, &quot;thanks for the help, now get out&quot;. They do not care about their apps. They are meat. And once those apps help their guild accomplish their goal for that particular app run (1st app run was to beat Coirnav/Rathe, this one is to beat Quarm, 3ish months and counting), there&#039;s a very good chance those apps will be sent packing again. <br /><br />I&#039;m not posting this stuff to slam Conviction, really I&#039;m not. Like I said, our 2 guilds have had solid relations for some time. But, in the event that any or all of those rumors are true, I want people to know that the situation there will not be all rosy and perfect like they will make it out to be. They don&#039;t care what happens to the apps as long as they help them kill Quarm. <br /><br />Now, Hegemony opened up apps to help us get over a hump too of course, ours being Xegony, Coirnav and Rathe. Both guilds had and have goals in mind, reasons that they opened recruitment. The difference between the 2 guilds being that Hegemony cares about it&#039;s apps, Conviction does not. Hegemony is fully flagging our apps. Hegemony will not deguild you simply because a particular goal gets met. We know how important our apps are and how pivotal they are in getting us to Quarm and beyond. Anyone that helps us acheive these goals - full members and apps alike - are considered part of the Heg family and will be treated as such. /hugglez <br /><br />3 rounds of thanks here.. <br /><br />Thanks to you apps and newer members for choosing Hegemony to spend your time with, you will not be disappointed. <br /><br />Thanks to you old school Heg peeps who have stuck it out over the last several months, however painful it may have been. You stayed with us during our bleakest days and are now seeing the fruits of all the hard work you have put in. <br /><br />And finally, thanks to everyone for making Hegemony the best damn guild on the server and keeping us there. Sure, there have been bumps on the way and I imagine there will be a few more but we&#039;ve always, always, always fought through it and came out better on the other side. Thank you so much. <br /><br />/cheer hegemony. Pat yourselves on the back, it&#039;s well deserved but don&#039;t get complacent or relaxed just yet.. <br /><br />You ain&#039;t seen nothin&#039; yet. <br /><br />Last edited by Daarksun on Fri Aug 13, 2004 9:10 am; edited 1 time in total<br /><br /><br />
